<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁβρ-ύνω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁβρός</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make delicate, treat
				delicately,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ γυναικὸς ἐν τρόποις ἐμὲ
				ἅβρυνε&lt;&gt;</span> A <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				919
			</span></i>: <i>deck out,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς γάμον ἁβρῦναί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.281
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>):—
				Med.
			 or 
				Pass.
			, <i>live delicately</i>; hence, <i>wax wanton, give
				oneself airs,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁβρύνεται γὰρ πᾶς τις εὖ πράσσων
					πλέον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1205
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1339
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκαλλυνόμην τε καὶ ἡβρυνόμην ἄν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					20c
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. rei, <i>pride, plume oneself on a</i> thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ ἁβρύνομαι τῷδ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					858
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡβρύνετο τῷ βραδέως διαπράττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					9.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷς ὁ τῶν γυναικῶν ἁβρύνεται βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Clearch.
					9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
